---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Cta from '../components/Cta.astro';
import { BROKER, SITE, DISCLAIMER_LONG } from '../config/site';

const paragraphs = DISCLAIMER_LONG.split('\n\n');
---

<Base
  title="About — Jordan Buttarazzi, Broker"
  description="Jordan Buttarazzi, Broker with Valery Real Estate Inc., Brokerage. RECO #5009855. Independent buyer representation for Ontario pre-construction low-rise: detached homes, townhomes and semis."
  kicker={['Ontario', 'Low-rise', 'About']}
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Home', href: '/' }, { name: 'About', href: '/about' }]}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-[1100px] px-4 pt-8 sm:px-6">
    <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-x-12">
      <div class="lg:col-span-7">
        <p class="section-label">— About</p>
        <h1 class="mt-4 text-[1.95rem] leading-[1.1] font-semibold sm:text-[2.4rem]">
          {BROKER.name}, {BROKER.title}
        </h1>
        <p class="lede mt-6">
          I represent buyers of new freehold low-rise homes in Ontario — detached, townhomes and
          semis. Not condos. The site exists because pre-construction is sold with urgency and
          bought with incomplete information, and the gap between those two things costs people
          real money.
        </p>

        <div class="prose-precon mt-8">
          <h2>Why low-rise only</h2>
          <p>
            Most pre-construction advice online is written about condominiums, because that is
            where the volume and the marketing budgets are. Low-rise is a different transaction
            with different risks, and some of them are worse.
          </p>
          <p>
            A freehold buyer gets <strong>no cooling-off period</strong> — the ten-day rescission
            right everyone has heard about is a condominium provision. A freehold buyer's deposit
            protection caps at 10% of the price up to $100,000, with no trust protection layer. A
            freehold buyer pays development levies and connection charges a condo buyer never
            sees. And a freehold buyer is usually making a larger purchase with less mandated
            disclosure.
          </p>
          <p>
            Those are the things I spend my time on, so narrowing the focus made more sense than
            pretending to cover everything.
          </p>

          <h2>What I actually do</h2>
          <p>
            Read the agreement commercially alongside your lawyer's legal review — the HST rebate
            clause, the levy cap, the deposit schedule, the assignment rights. Tell you what a
            builder's delivery record and date reliability actually look like. Tell you which lots
            and premiums are worth paying for and which are not. Tell you when a release is not
            worth your time.
          </p>
          <p>
            The builder budgets a co-operating brokerage commission whether or not you bring
            representation. If you walk in alone, they keep it — the price does not drop. So
            having someone whose obligation is to you costs you nothing.{' '}
            <a href="/faq/does-it-cost-more-to-use-a-realtor-precon">The economics</a>.
          </p>

          <h2>What I don't do</h2>
          <p>
            I am a licensed real estate Broker. I am <strong>not</strong> a lawyer, an accountant
            or a mortgage agent, and I will not pretend otherwise. The content on this site
            explains published program rules — CRA notices, Tarion's coverage terms, the
            Condominium Act's rescission provisions — and cites its sources so you can check it.
          </p>
          <p>
            Where a question turns on the law or on your tax position, you will be told to take it
            to the right professional. That is not a disclaimer for its own sake. A rebate worth up
            to $80,000 that gets billed back to you at closing is not something to resolve from a
            web page.
          </p>

          <h2>Where I work</h2>
          <p>
            New low-rise communities across the Greater Toronto Area — York Region, Peel, Halton
            and Durham. {SITE.domain} covers the questions that come up most, and the{' '}
            <a href="/hst-rebate/checker">rebate checker</a> gives you an estimate in about two
            minutes.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <aside class="lg:col-span-5">
        <div class="tick-corners card p-5">
          <p class="section-label">— Registration</p>
          <!-- RECO: brokerage name at least as prominent as the individual's. -->
          <p class="mt-3 text-[15px] font-semibold text-ink">{BROKER.brokerage}</p>
          <p class="text-[15px] text-ink/80">{BROKER.name}, {BROKER.title}</p>
          <dl class="mt-4 space-y-2 border-t border-rule pt-4 text-[13px]">
            <div class="flex gap-3">
              <dt class="w-24 shrink-0 text-ink/55">RECO</dt>
              <dd class="figure text-ink">#{BROKER.reco}</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="flex gap-3">
              <dt class="w-24 shrink-0 text-ink/55">Phone</dt>
              <dd>
                <a href={BROKER.phoneHref} class="figure text-accent underline underline-offset-2">
                  {BROKER.phone}
                </a>
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div class="flex gap-3">
              <dt class="w-24 shrink-0 text-ink/55">Email</dt>
              <dd>
                <a href={`mailto:${BROKER.email}`} class="text-accent underline underline-offset-2">
                  {BROKER.email}
                </a>
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div class="flex gap-3">
              <dt class="w-24 shrink-0 text-ink/55">Serves</dt>
              <dd class="text-ink/80">{BROKER.areaServed}</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="flex gap-3">
              <dt class="w-24 shrink-0 text-ink/55">Focus</dt>
              <dd class="text-ink/80">Freehold low-rise — detached, towns, semis</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-6 border border-rule bg-accent-tint/40 p-5">
          <p class="section-label">— Disclaimer</p>
          <div class="mt-2 space-y-3 text-[12px] leading-relaxed text-ink/70">
            {paragraphs.map((p) => <p>{p}</p>)}
          </div>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>

    <Cta />
  </div>
</Base>
